H6100.definition:
from H6096 (עָצֶה) and H1397 (גֶּבֶר); backbone-like of a man;
Etsjon-Geber, a place on the Red Sea
KJV: Ezion-geber.

H6101.definition:
a primitive root;
to lean idly, i.e. to be indolent or slack
KJV: be slothful.

H6102.definition:
from H6101 (עָצַל);
indolent
KJV: slothful, sluggard.

H6103.definition:
feminine of H6102 (עָצֵל);
(as abstractly) indolence
KJV: slothfulness.

H6106.definition:
from H6105 (עָצַם);
a bone (as strong); by extension, the body; figuratively, the substance, i.e. (as pron.) selfsame
KJV: body, bone, [idiom] life, (self-) same, strength, [idiom] very.

H6107.definition:
the same as H6106 (עֶצֶם); bone;
Etsem, a place in Palestine
KJV: Azem, Ezem.

H6108.definition:
from H6105 (עָצַם);
power; hence, body
KJV: might, strong, substance.

H6109.definition:
feminine of H6108 (עֹצֶם);
powerfulness; by extension, numerousness
KJV: abundance, strength.

H6110.definition:
feminine of H6099 (עָצוּם);
a bulwark, i.e. (figuratively) argument
KJV: strong.

H6111.definition:
or עַצְמֹן; from H6107 (עֶצֶם); bone-like;
Atsmon, a place near Palestine
KJV: Azmon.

H6112.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be sharp or strong;
a spear
KJV: Eznite (from the margin).

H6113.definition:
a primitive root;
to inclose; by analogy, to hold back; also to maintain, rule, assemble
KJV: [idiom] be able, close up, detain, fast, keep (self close, still), prevail, recover, refrain, [idiom] reign, restrain, retain, shut (up), slack, stay, stop, withhold (self).

H6115.definition:
from H6113 (עָצָר);
closure; also constraint
KJV: [idiom] barren, oppression, [idiom] prison.

H6116.definition:
or עֲצֶרֶת; from H6113 (עָצָר);
an assembly, especially on afestival or holiday
KJV: (solemn) assembly (meeting).

H6118.definition:
from H6117 (עָקַב) in the sense of H6119 (עָקֵב);
a heel, i.e. (figuratively) the last of anything (used adverbially, for ever); also result, i.e. compensation; and so (adverb with preposition or relatively) on account of
KJV: [idiom] because, by, end, for, if, reward.

H6119.definition:
or (feminine) עִקְּבָה; from H6117 (עָקַב);
a heel (as protuberant); hence, a track; figuratively, the rear (of an army)
KJV: heel, (horse-) hoof, last, lier in wait (by mistake for H6120 (עָקֵב)), (foot-) step.

H6120.definition:
from H6117 (עָקַב) in its denominative sense;
a lier in wait
KJV: heel (by mistake for H6119 (עָקֵב)).

H6122.definition:
feminine of an unused form from H6117 (עָקַב) meaning a trick;
trickery
KJV: subtilty.

H6123.definition:
a primitive root;
to tie with thongs
KJV: bind.

H6124.definition:
from H6123 (עָקַד);
striped (with bands)
KJV: ring straked.

H6126.definition:
from H6117 (עָקַב); insidious;
Akkub, the name of five Israelites
KJV: Akkub.

H6127.definition:
a primitive root;
to wrest
KJV: wrong.

H6128.definition:
from H6127 (עָקַל);
winding
KJV: by(-way), crooked way.

H6130.definition:
from an unused root meaning to twist; tortuous;
Akan, an Idummaean
KJV: Akan. Compare H3292 (יַעֲקָן).

H6131.definition:
a primitive root;
to pluck up (especially by the roots); specifically, to hamstring; figuratively, to exterminate
KJV: dig down, hough, pluck up, root up.

H6132.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6131 (עָקַר)
{to pluck up (especially by the roots); specifically, to hamstring; figuratively, to exterminate}
KJV: pluck up by the roots.

H6133.definition:
from H6131 (עָקַר);
figuratively, a transplanted person, i.e. naturalized citizen
KJV: stock.

H6134.definition:
the same as H6133 (עֵקֶר);
Eker, an Israelite
KJV: Eker.

H6135.definition:
from H6131 (עָקַר);
sterile (as if extirpated in the generative organs)
KJV: ([idiom] male or female) barren (woman).

H6136.definition:
(Aramaic) from H6132 (עֲקַר);
a stock
KJV: stump.

H6137.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a scorpion; figuratively, a scourge or knotted whip
KJV: scorpion.

H6138.definition:
from H6131 (עָקַר); eradication;
Ekron, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ekron.

H6139.definition:
or עֶקְרֹנִי; patrial from H6138 (עֶקְרוֹן);
an Ekronite or inhabitant of Ekron
KJV: Ekronite.

H6140.definition:
a primitive root;
to knot or distort; figuratively, to pervert (act or declare perverse)
KJV: make crooked, (prove, that is) perverse(-rt).

H6141.definition:
from H6140 (עָקַשׁ);
distorted; hence, false
KJV: crooked, froward, perverse.

H6142.definition:
the same as H6141 (עִקֵּשׁ); perverse;
Ikkesh, an Israelite
KJV: Ikkesh.

H6144.definition:
the same as H5892 (עִיר); a city;
Ar, a place in Moab
KJV: Ar.

H6145.definition:
from H5782 (עוּר);
a foe (as watchful for mischief)
KJV: enemy.

H6146.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6145 (עָר)
{a foe (as watchful for mischief)}
KJV: enemy.

H6147.definition:
from H5782 (עוּר); watchful;
Er, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Er.

H6148.definition:
a primitive root;
to braid, i.e. intermix; technically, to traffic (as if by barter); also or give to be security (as a kind of exchange)
KJV: engage, (inter-) meddle (with), mingle (self), mortgage, occupy, give pledges, be(-come, put in) surety, undertake.

H6149.definition:
a primitive root (rather identical with H6148 (עָרַב) through the idea of close association);
to be agreeable
KJV: be pleasant(-ing), take pleasure in, be sweet.

H6150.definition:
a primitive root (rather identical with H6148 (עָרַב) through the idea of covering with a texture);
to grow dusky at sundown
KJV: be darkened, (toward) evening.

H6151.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6148 (עָרַב);
to commingle
KJV: mingle (self), mix.

H6152.definition:
or עֲרַב; from H6150 (עָרַב) in the figurative sense of sterility;
Arab (i.e. Arabia), a country East of Palestine
KJV: Arabia.

H6153.definition:
from H6150 (עָרַב);
dusk
KJV: [phrase] day, even(-ing, tide), night.

H6154.definition:
or עֶרֶב; (1 Kings 10:15), (with the article [prefix), from H6148 (עָרַב);
the web (or transverse threads of cloth); also a mixture, (or mongrel race)
KJV: Arabia, mingled people, mixed (multitude), woof.

H6155.definition:
from H6148 (עָרַב);
a willow (from the use of osiers as wattles)
KJV: willow.

H6157.definition:
from H6148 (עָרַב);
a mosquito (from its swarming)
KJV: divers sorts of flies, swarm.

H6158.definition:
or עוֹרֵב; from H6150 (עָרַב);
a raven (from its dusky hue)
KJV: raven.

H6159.definition:
or עוֹרֵב; the same as H6158 (עֹרֵב);
Oreb, the name of a Midianite and of the cliff near the Jordan
KJV: Oreb.

H6160.definition:
from H6150 (עָרַב) (in the sense of sterility);
a desert; especially (with the article prefix) the (generally) sterile valley of the Jordan and its continuation to the Red Sea
KJV: Arabah, champaign, desert, evening, heaven, plain, wilderness. See also H1026 (בֵּית הָעֲרָבָה).

H6161.definition:
feminine passive participle of H6048 (עֲנַמֶּלֶךְ) in the sense of a bargain or exchange;
something given as security, i.e. (literally) a token (of safety) or (metaphorically) a bondsman
KJV: pledge, surety.

H6162.definition:
from H6148 (עָרַב) (in the sense of exchange);
a pawn (given as security)
KJV: pledge.

H6163.definition:
or עַרְבִי; patrial from H6152 (עֲרָב);
an Arabian or inhabitant of Arab (i.e. Arabia)
KJV: Arabian.

H6164.definition:
patrial from H1026 (בֵּית הָעֲרָבָה);
an Arbathite or inhabitant of (Beth-) Arabah
KJV: Arbahite.

H6165.definition:
a primitive root;
to long for
KJV: cry, pant.

H6166.definition:
from an unused root meaning to sequester itself; fugitive;
Arad, the name of a place near Palestine, also of a Canaanite and an Israelite
KJV: Arad.

H6167.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6171 (עָרוֹד);
an onager
KJV: wild ass.

H6168.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (causatively, make) bare; hence, to empty, pour out, demolish
KJV: leave destitute, discover, empty, make naked, pour (out), rase, spread self, uncover.

H6169.definition:
feminine from H6168 (עָרָה);
a naked (i.e. level) plot
KJV: paper reed.

H6170.definition:
or עֲרֻגָה; feminine passive participle of H6165 (עָרַג);
something piled up (as if (figuratively) raised by mental aspiration), i.e. a paterre
KJV: bed, furrow.

H6171.definition:
from the same as H6166 (עֲרָד);
an onager (from his lonesome habits)
KJV: wild ass.

H6172.definition:
from H6168 (עָרָה);
nudity, literally (especially the pudenda) or figuratively (disgrace, blemish)
KJV: nakedness, shame, unclean(-ness).

H6173.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6172 (עֶרְוָה);
nakedness, i.e. (figuratively) impoverishment
KJV: dishonor.

H6174.definition:
or עָרֹם; from H6191 (עָרַם) (in its original sense);
nude, either partially or totally
KJV: naked.

H6175.definition:
passive participle of H6191 (עָרַם);
cunning (usually in a bad sense)
KJV: crafty, prudent, subtil.

H6176.definition:
or עַרְעָר; from H6209 (עָרַר) reduplicated;
a juniper (from its nudity of situation)
KJV: health.

H6177.definition:
or עֲרֹעֵר; or עַרְעוֹר; the same as H6176 (עֲרוֹעֵר); nudity of situation;
Aroer, the name of three places in or near Palestine
KJV: Aroer.

H6178.definition:
passive participle of H6206 (עָרַץ);
feared, i.e. (concretely) a horrible place or chasm
KJV: cliffs.

H6179.definition:
from H5782 (עוּר); watchful;
Eri, an Israelite
KJV: Eri.

H6180.definition:
patronymically of H6179 (עֵרִי);
a Erite (collectively) or descendants of Eri
KJV: Erites.

H6181.definition:
for H6172 (עֶרְוָה);
nudity
KJV: bare, naked, [idiom] quite.

H6182.definition:
from an unused root meaning to comminute;
meal
KJV: dough.

H6183.definition:
from H6201 (עָרַף);
the sky (as dropping at the horizon)
KJV: heaven.

H6184.definition:
from H6206 (עָרַץ);
fearful, i.e. powerful or tyrannical
KJV: mighty, oppressor, in great power, strong, terrible, violent.

H6185.definition:
from H6209 (עָרַר);
bare, i.e. destitute (of children)
KJV: childless.

H6186.definition:
a primitive root;
to set in a row, i.e. arrange, put in order (in a very wide variety of applications)
KJV: put (set) (the battle, self) in array, compare, direct, equal, esteem, estimate, expert (in war), furnish, handle, join (battle), ordain, (lay, put, reckon up, set) (in) order, prepare, tax, value.

H6187.definition:
from H6186 (עָרַךְ);
a pile, equipment, estimate
KJV: equal, estimation, (things that are set in) order, price, proportion, [idiom] set at, suit, taxation, [idiom] valuest.

H6188.definition:
a primitive root; properly, to strip; but used as denominative from H6189 (עָרֵל);
to expose or remove the prepuce, whether literal (to go naked) or figurative (to refrain from using)
KJV: count uncircumcised, foreskin to be uncovered.

H6189.definition:
from H6188 (עָרֵל); properly, exposed, i.e. projecting loose (as to the prepuce); used only technically,
uncircumcised (i.e. still having the prepuce uncurtailed)
KJV: uncircumcised (person).

H6190.definition:
feminine of H6189 (עָרֵל);
the prepuce
KJV: foreskin, [phrase] uncircumcised.

H6191.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be (or make) bare; but used only in the derivative sense (through the idea perhaps of smoothness) to be cunning (usually in a bad sense)
KJV: [idiom] very, beware, take crafty (counsel), be prudent, deal subtilly.

H6192.definition:
a primitive root;
to pile up
KJV: gather together.

H6193.definition:
from H6191 (עָרַם);
a stratagem
KJV: craftiness.

H6194.definition:
(Jeremiah 50:26) or (feminine) עֲרֵמָה; from H6192 (עָרַם);
a heap; specifically, a sheaf
KJV: heap (of corn), sheaf.

H6195.definition:
feminine of H6193 (עֹרֶם);
trickery; or (in a good sense) discretion
KJV: guile, prudence, subtilty, wilily, wisdom.

H6196.definition:
probably from H6191 (עָרַם);
the plane tree (from its smooth and shed bark)
KJV: chestnut tree.

H6197.definition:
probably from H5782 (עוּר); watchful;
Eran, an Israelite
KJV: Eran.

H6198.definition:
patronymically from H6197 (עֵרָן);
an Eranite or descendant (collectively) of Eran
KJV: Eranites.

H6199.definition:
from H6209 (עָרַר);
naked, i.e. (figuratively) poor
KJV: destitute. See also H6176 (עֲרוֹעֵר).
